md`# Three languages in one module

The cells on this page are written in three languages and read each other. \`width\` and \`doubledWidth\` are SoundScript. \`viewof height\` and \`summary\` are Observable JavaScript. \`area\`, \`squares\` and \`report\` are raw cells: a name, a list of inputs and a function, which is what the runtime stores for any cell.`
// %%
polyglot_listing = cellListing(polyglot_module, invalidation)
// %%
//ss: ./sections/polyglot.ts -fromRaw
// %%
viewof height = Inputs.range([1, 10], { value: 3, step: 1, label: "height" })
// %%
define("area", ["width", "height"], function (width, height) {
  // a raw cell: the function as written, its inputs as listed
  return width * height;
})
// %%
define("squares", ["area"], function* (area) {
  for (let i = 1; i <= area; i++) yield i * i;
})
// %%
define("report", ["area", "squares"], async (area, squares) => `area ${area}, last square ${squares}`)
// %%
summary = md`${report}; the SoundScript cell \`doubledWidth\` is ${doubledWidth}.`
// %%
md`Move the slider. \`area\` is a raw cell that reads a SoundScript cell and an Observable JavaScript control. \`summary\` is an Observable JavaScript cell that reads a raw cell and a SoundScript cell.`
// %%
md`## How a language is added

A language is a module that registers on the \`cell_languages\` point of the cell map. It gives \`decompile\`, which turns a stored cell back into source, and \`apply\`, which stores an edit, and it marks each cell it stores with a comment naming the language. The editor, the visualizer and the listing ask the registry. None of them names a language.`
// %%
md`## Choosing a language

The editor's header has a picker that shows the language a cell will be stored in. A new cell starts in the language of the cell it was added after. Typing text that only one registered language accepts, and that Observable JavaScript does not parse, switches the picker to that language. \`define(…)\` is a valid Observable JavaScript expression, so it does not switch: pick \`raw\`, or add the cell after a raw cell.`
// %%
md`The listing leaves out \`viewof height\` and \`summary\`. Observable JavaScript is built into the editor and is not a registered language.`
// %%
md`A SoundScript cell cannot read a raw or Observable JavaScript cell yet: \`fromRaw\` is rejected with \`[inject-unknown]\`.`
// %%
//ss: ./sections/polyglot.ts -width -doubledWidth
// %%
test_polyglot_listing = {
  // the listing is drawn after each code change; it is read once it has the last raw cell. A listing replaced
  // before it is drawn is never drawn, and the runtime runs this cell again only once this run ends, so the wait
  // also ends on invalidation
  const has = () => polyglot_listing.textContent.includes('define("report"');
  if (!has()) await new Promise((resolve) => {
    const mo = new MutationObserver(() => { if (has()) { mo.disconnect(); resolve(); } });
    mo.observe(polyglot_listing, { childList: true, subtree: true, characterData: true });
    invalidation.then(() => { mo.disconnect(); resolve(); });
  });
  const text = polyglot_listing.textContent;
  for (const want of ["const width = () => 4;", "const fromRaw = (area: number) => area + 1;", 'define("area", ["width", "height"]']) if (!text.includes(want)) throw new Error(`the listing has no ${want}`);
  for (const not of ["Inputs.range", "summary"]) if (text.includes(not)) throw new Error(`the listing has ${not}`);
  return "the listing has the SoundScript and raw cells and leaves out viewof height and summary";
}
// %%
test_polyglot_fromRaw_rejected = {
  try { await polyglot_module.value("fromRaw"); } catch (e) {
    if (/^fromRaw does not check: \[inject-unknown\]/.test(e.message)) return e.message;
    throw e;
  }
  throw new Error("fromRaw ran");
}
// %%
viewof polyglot_module = thisModule()
// %%
import { ss, cellListing } from "@tomlarkworthy/soundscript"
// %%
import { thisModule } from "@tomlarkworthy/runtime-sdk"
